.TH DCC_FAN 4 2026-11-26 "Dudes Control Center @VERSION@" "Kernel Interfaces"
.nh
.SH NAME
dcc_fan \- fan and temperature kernel module for Clevo notebooks
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B modprobe dcc_fan
.RB [ method=auto | wmi | ec ]
.RI [ watchdog_sec=N ]
.RB [ force=1 ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dcc_fan
gives
.BR dcc-fan-daemon (8)
and
.BR dcc-fan-cli (1)
access to the fans and temperatures of Clevo notebooks through the kernel,
instead of the programs writing to the embedded controller's I/O ports
0x62/0x66 themselves.
The package builds it with DKMS (together with
.BR ite_829x )
and loads it at boot.
The programs use it when it is loaded; without it they use direct port I/O
only if the administrator allowed it
.RB ( "dcc-component ec-direct enable" )
and the EC answers like a Clevo EC.
Their status shows which is in use.
.PP
Compared with port I/O from user space:
.IP \(bu 2
the EC is read through the kernel's ACPI EC driver, under the same lock the
firmware's own EC accesses use, so the two cannot interleave;
.IP \(bu 2
no
.BR ioperm (2)
is needed, which kernel lockdown (usually on with Secure Boot) forbids;
.IP \(bu 2
the fan duty that is shown is the one the firmware reports through Clevo's
WMI interface (some ECs leave the duty registers at 0);
.IP \(bu 2
temperatures and fans appear in standard tools such as
.BR sensors (1);
.IP \(bu 2
a watchdog in the kernel sets the fans to 100\~% when the controlling
program stops sending updates.
.PP
The module loads only where Clevo's WMI interface
(GUID ABBC0F6D-8EA1-11D1-00A0-C90629100000) exists, unless
.BR force=1 .
.SH HWMON INTERFACE
The module registers a hwmon device named
.BR dcc_fan :
.TP
.BR temp1_input ", " temp2_input
CPU and GPU temperature in millidegrees Celsius (EC registers 0x07, 0xCD);
labels CPU and GPU.
.TP
.BR fan1_input ", " fan2_input
CPU and GPU fan speed in RPM (EC registers 0xD0/0xD1, 0xD2/0xD3).
.TP
.BR pwm1 ", " pwm2
Fan duty 0\-255.
Reading gives the duty the firmware runs (WMI GET_FANINFO1/2, byte 0).
Writing (root only) sets it.
Very low values can stop a fan; on the X58xWNx below about 31 (12\~%).
.SH PARAMETERS
.TP
.BR method= auto | wmi | ec
How the fan speed is set: Clevo WMI SET_FANSPEED_VALUE (0x68) or EC command
0x99 through the kernel's EC driver; auto (default) uses WMI when present.
.TP
.BI watchdog_sec= N
Once a duty was written, the fans go to 100\~% when no write comes for
.I N
seconds (default 30, 0 = off).
.BR dcc-fan-daemon (8)
writes every 5 seconds.
Unloading the module also sets 100\~% if it had set a duty.
.TP
.B force=1
Load without the Clevo WMI interface (EC only).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /sys/devices/platform/dcc_fan/control
Method in use, last duties written, watchdog state.
.TP
.I /sys/devices/platform/dcc_fan/wmi_faninfo
Raw results of the WMI fan information commands.
.TP
.I /sys/devices/platform/dcc_fan/ec_values
The EC values the module reads.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/modules-load.d/dudes-control-center.conf
Loads the module at boot.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dudes-control-center (7),
.BR dcc-fan-daemon (8),
.BR dcc-fan-cli (1),
.BR sensors (1)
